# Copy this file to tools/denylist.local.txt and fill in your own project's
# sensitive proper nouns: a company name, a product name, a person's name, a
# private vault's folder name — anything check-purity.py's public *shape*
# patterns can't catch because it doesn't name a specific real entity.
#
# tools/denylist.local.txt is gitignored, so your private terms never ship —
# only this .example file (generic placeholders, safe to publish) is tracked.
#
# Format: one term per line, case-insensitive substring match, "#" for
# comments, blank lines ignored. Prefer specific multi-word or compound terms
# over a single common word or bare first name — a short common word will
# false-positive on unrelated text (see check-purity.py's own CLEAN test
# cases for examples of exactly that trap).
#
# acme-corp
# acme's internal wiki
# ada-lovelace-project
# example-vault-name
# secret-codename
